{"counts":{"allowed":1,"error":1,"info":1,"review":4,"suppressed":2,"warn":3},"groups":[{"files":{"a.txt":[["1:1","custom finding","c8dfae3"]]},"rule":"acme/custom","severity":"error"},{"expected":"package sample\n\nfunc Helper() {}","files":{"bar/bar.go":[["4:1","exported function Func1 must have a doc comment","adc7d1d"],["7:1","exported function Func2 must have a doc comment","ab2cb8c",{"evidence":{"receiver":"T"},"note":"judgment expired: decision changed"}]]},"requirement":"Exported symbols SHOULD have doc comments in the language's standard form. Public API changes SHOULD document user-visible behavior, constraints, ownership, or other facts the code cannot express.","review":true,"rule":"design/exported-doc","severity":"warn"},{"evidence":{"callees":["a","b c"],"fan_in":2,"fan_out":14,"symbol":"jit::compile#function"},"expected":"package sample\n\nfunc total(a, b int) int {\n    sum := a\n\n    sum += b\n\n    return sum\n}","files":{"internal/jit/compile.go":[["350:1","function coordinates 14 collaborators in its package","95c1bd4"]]},"requirement":"A function SHOULD NOT exceed the limit of its role in lines, statements, cyclomatic complexity, cognitive complexity or nesting depth, and SHOULD NOT be a dependency hub or a high fan-out coordinator. Cyclomatic complexity is one path plus each `if`, `else if`, loop, error handler clause, non-default switch arm and boolean operator (`&&`, `||`). The remedy is simpler code or a concept that is reused, never the same body moved elsewhere. One function MUST stay at one abstraction level: intent and mechanics are not mixed in one body, so that it reads as a sequence of steps one level below its name. Mechanical checks SHOULD be preferred for directly expressible rules; heuristic signals SHOULD remain advisory and use deliberately high thresholds.","review":true,"rule":"design/complexity","severity":"warn"},{"authored":"warn","expected":"#[derive(PartialEq)]\npub enum Failure {\n    Missing,\n}\n\npub fn is_missing(err: &Failure) -> bool {\n    *err == Failure::Missing\n}","files":{"src/lib.rs":[["7:1","private helper has one caller","46aa779"]]},"requirement":"Dependency identity MUST be preserved when callers depend on it; context added to an error MUST keep the cause reachable: an error MUST be compared with `errors.Is`, asserted with `errors.As` and wrapped with `%w`. Semantic errors MUST use stable, named error values or types, and semantic categories MUST NOT be created from ad hoc formatted messages alone. Error categories MUST be translated only at their owning boundary. Errors MUST NOT expose private or sensitive process state. Panic MUST be limited to impossible programmer errors, `Must*`-style APIs, or documented hot-path invariants with one recovery boundary; normal runtime failures MUST return errors.","review":true,"rule":"design/errors","severity":"info"}],"incomplete":[["broken.go","type error"]],"judgments":{"fail":"the finding is right; add `suppress` with a justification to leave it in place","notApplicable":"the decision does not apply here; a hint to narrow it","pass":"false positive: the code conforms"},"resolve":"review_resolve {fingerprint, judgment, suppress?, reason?}","status":"incomplete"}
